Subject: [GTK] Use damage for compositing by default

Draft against the webkitgtk-2.52.6 release tarball. Apply with -p1 from the
tarball root. Independent of the other drafts. Compiled and measured (dev/bench/RESULTS.md).

What it does
  Makes UseDamagingInformationForCompositing default to true for the WebKit
  frontend on GTK, as 2.54 does (2.54 yaml: "PLATFORM(GTK) || PLATFORM(WPE)").
  With the flag on, ThreadedCompositor::paintToCurrentGLContext() scissors the
  clear and the layer tree paint to the bounding box of the damage accumulated
  for the current render target (ThreadedCompositor.cpp:293-303).

Why a default and not the public API
  The flag is sampled once, in the LayerTreeHost constructor
  (LayerTreeHost.cpp:100-110), which runs inside the WebPage constructor
  (WebPage.cpp:958 then :980). A value set with
  webkit_settings_set_feature_enabled() after the first load reaches the web
  process in a PreferencesDidChange message, after the LayerTreeHost exists,
  and is never read again.

What it does not handle
  - The flag is still not re-read at runtime.
  - Composition is restricted to ONE bounding box (the per-target record is
    Damage::Mode::BoundingBox, AcceleratedSurface.cpp:1079). Two small
    animations far apart damage the box that contains both.
  - glReadPixels and the UI process redraw stay full size (see 0003, 0004).
  - WPE is left unchanged.

--- a/Source/WTF/Scripts/Preferences/UnifiedWebPreferences.yaml
+++ b/Source/WTF/Scripts/Preferences/UnifiedWebPreferences.yaml
@@ -8561,6 +8561,7 @@
     WebKitLegacy:
       default: false
     WebKit:
+      "PLATFORM(GTK)": true
       default: false
     WebCore:
       default: false
